1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,640
Being in your 20 s is a confusing and turbulent time.
二十多岁，是一段令人困惑、动荡不定的时光。

2
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:12,110
However I must say that I find myself super lucky that while I do have problems and they can feel like they are horrible and that my world is just spinning upside down.
不过她必须说，自己很幸运：虽然确实有问题，而且可能感觉糟透了，仿佛整个世界都翻转失序——

3
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:16,480
However I don't have to worry about problems that are actively threatening my life or livelihood.
但她不必担心那些直接威胁生命或生计的问题。

4
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:21,519
I can't imagine being in my 20 s and also being faced with homelessness or addiction.
她无法想象，在二十多岁时还要面对无家可归或成瘾。

5
00:00:21,519 --> 00:00:27,320
So while I may be somewhat complaining in the next part of this video I don't want to be taken that I'm ungrateful.
所以，接下来她也许会抱怨，但她不希望被理解为不知感恩。

6
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:31,440
I just want to point that out before I go further because I know that some people have it worse from me.
在继续之前，她想先说明这一点，因为她知道有些人的处境比她更差。〔from me 原字幕搭配疑点，待复核〕

7
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:35,760
But also I don't think that diminishes my problems I have in my own life now back to me complaining.
但她也不认为这会减轻自己生活中的问题。好，回到她的抱怨。

8
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:41,880
Some people of the older generation or society as a whole have this unrealistic idea of what someone should be doing in their 20 s.
一些上一代的人，或整个社会，对一个人二十多岁时该做什么，有不切实际的想象。

9
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:47,480
Which then makes everyone in their 20 s feel like they're epically failing because they're not living up to this expectation.
这让二十多岁的人觉得自己一败涂地，因为没有达到那种期待。

10
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:50,640
This is a reminder only made worse by social media.
这种提醒又因社交媒体而变得更糟。

11
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:55,719
Having the ability to compare yourself to the lives of people who have their way more together than you do.
你可以把自己和那些生活比你井井有条得多的人作比较——〔have their way more together 原字幕疑似漏词，待复核〕

12
00:00:55,719 --> 00:01:00,670
Or at least they appear like they have their way more together than you do it's even worse when they're younger than you.
或者，至少他们看起来比你更有条理；如果他们还比你年轻，那就更难受了。

13
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:02,519
Comparison is the thief of joy.
比较是快乐的窃贼。

14
00:01:02,519 --> 00:01:07,519
But I think a lot of people can't avoid the feeling that they should have the perfect job or a great relationship.
但她觉得，很多人无法摆脱那种感觉：自己应该拥有完美的工作，或很好的伴侣关系。

15
00:01:07,519 --> 00:01:10,640
The cost of housing is increasing while wages stay similar.
她说，住房成本在上升，工资却差不多没变。

16
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:13,279
College feels almost like a necessity to have a career.
大学几乎像是拥有一份职业的必需条件。

17
00:01:13,279 --> 00:01:17,640
But then at the same time will put you into mountains of debt that'll take you years to pay off.
可与此同时，它又会让你背上山一样的债务，花上多年才能还清。

18
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:19,760
And now we have the loneliness epidemic.
而现在，还有所谓的“孤独流行”。

19
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:26,480
In 1990 around the time when my parents bought their house it was more typical not totally typical but more typical.
1990 年前后，她父母买房时，有一种情况更常见——并非完全普遍，只是更常见。

20
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:28,719
For only one person in a partnership to work.
那就是，伴侣中只有一人工作——

21
00:01:28,719 --> 00:01:34,000
While the other person would be able to stay home and still afford a house and maybe even afford a child.
另一人能待在家中，同时还买得起房，甚至养得起一个孩子。

22
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,440
But now most couples even if they both work still seem really can't afford to buy a house.
可现在，大多数伴侣即使双方都工作，似乎仍买不起房。

23
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:44,159
And that's not even considering people that are single like no shot you're going to be able to buy a house unless you make a lot of money.
这还没算单身的人；她说，除非你赚很多钱，否则根本没戏买房。

24
00:01:44,159 --> 00:01:47,000
I was going to try and insert some statistics here.
她原本想在这里插入一些统计数据。

25
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,079
But do I really need to put some numbers on the screen for you to agree.
但她真的需要把数字放在屏幕上，才能让你认同吗——

26
00:01:50,079 --> 00:01:54,560
That americans are astronomically down bad when it comes to money right now I don't think so.
认同美国人现在在金钱方面窘迫得不得了？她觉得不需要。

27
00:01:54,560 --> 00:02:02,079
And even without statistics to depress me I feel like my parents generation and the generation before could rely on this idea that if you work hard enough.
即使没有统计数据让她沮丧，她仍觉得父母那一代和再上一代，可以依靠这样一种想法：只要足够努力——

28
00:02:02,079 --> 00:02:07,600
And stick to it that eventually you could hit these basic milestones like buying a house or starting a family.
并坚持下去，最终就能达到买房、组建家庭等基本人生节点。

29
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:12,079
But I feel like now even if it's a pessimistic mindset that I can't rely on this idea.
但她觉得如今，即使这是一种悲观看法，她也无法再依靠这种想法——

30
00:02:12,079 --> 00:02:14,560
That if I try hard life will work out for me.
也就是：只要努力，生活就会替自己变好。

31
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:20,120
Maybe what bothers me the most about this idea is that I really feel like there's no sense of security anymore.
也许最困扰她的是，她真的觉得不再有安全感。

32
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:24,079
I'm not trying to be dramatic but the anxiety that I get when I cau of work.
她不是想夸大，但当她请假不去工作时，会感到焦虑——〔cau of work 自动识别不清，按语境暂译，待听辨〕

33
00:02:24,079 --> 00:02:28,120
Or decide not to do a freelance project because I have other commitments already.
或者因为已有其他安排，决定不接一个自由职业项目时——

34
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:34,079
The anxiety is lethal because I can't help but wonder that oh in the future maybe I'm going to need that 100.
那焦虑简直要命，因为她忍不住想：将来，也许会需要那一百块钱。

35
00:02:34,079 --> 00:02:36,600
That I could have made working that random tuesday.
就是那个普通的星期二本来可以挣到的钱。

36
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:40,560
Or that oh if I would have taken that project maybe it would have opened me up to new opportunities.
或者，如果当时接下那个项目，也许它会为自己带来新的机会。

37
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:43,360
That I would finally be able to get a steady stable job.
也许自己终于能找到一份稳定的工作。

38
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:48,880
I'm just constantly in the state of feeling that everything that I've worked for is one day just going to randomly come to a halt.
她总处于这样的状态：觉得自己为之努力的一切，某天会突然停摆。

39
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:51,040
That the rug is going to be ripped underneath me.
仿佛脚下的地毯会突然被抽走。

40
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:57,440
I've seen just the other day people making videos talking about how degree they studied their whole life for that their funding was cut.
她前几天还看到有人发视频，说自己一辈子钻研的学位方向，其资助被砍掉了。

41
00:02:57,440 --> 00:03:00,159
And now it's like figure something else out.
现在就只能想别的办法。

42
00:03:00,159 --> 00:03:11,800
Like that's mind blowing to me that it can just be taken away even if you worked so hard.
这让她难以置信：即便你如此努力，一切仍可能被拿走。
